  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Demonstration of Incision Academy &amp; Assist for Surgical Workflow and Training Improvement in Kenya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Incision Group B.V. (Incision) designs digital surgical training and workflow tools aimed at improving the efficiency and safety of surgical procedures and standardisation in operating rooms. The goal is to deliver high-quality care.The Kenyan surgical healthcare system faces challenges such as a shortage of surgical staff, limited access to job-specific and accredited education, and significant variability in perioperative work processes between different facilities.Incision intends to demonstrate the integrated digital solution, consisting of  two platforms, at a Kenyan hospital, a recognised center for surgical training. The training content will be tailored to the local skills and knowledge gaps, already identified during the preparation phase. The expected export of digital surgical education and training is approximately &#x20ac;250,000 over 3 years.</narrative>
  </description>
